    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d866">

                <pb facs="0810" n="798" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg798"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751.90D11/10–944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Appointed Minister to Syria and Lebanon</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wadsworth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-09T20:00:00+02:00">October 9, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 9—3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. I hesitate to make verbal statement suggested in Department’s 177, October
                    7, 7 [<hi rendition="#italic">9</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="68" xml:id="d866-f1"/>
                    prior to learning something of Syrian Government reaction to Eden reply (Legtel
                    213, October 6, 8 p.m.) which is to be handed Foreign Minister this week.</p>
                <p>May I not therefore when presenting reply outlined in Department’s 176 October 7,
                    8 p.m. limit my remarks to inquiry as to whether the Minister believes more
                    favorable terms could be obtained now than later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wadsworth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
